# shellcheck config for the kernel-hive repo.
#
# Two gates read this file:
#   - .github/workflows/lint.yml    `shellcheck -S warning` (existing CI job)
#   - quality/bash's exit rule       `shellcheck $(git ls-files '*.sh')`
#     (full default severity — style/info/warning/error all shown; see
#     docs/lab/AGENT-CI-EXIT-RULE.md and AGENTS.md "Code quality gate")
#
# Repo-wide disables below are deliberate, documented exceptions — NOT a
# "quiet everything" list. Anything narrower is a scoped inline
# `# shellcheck disable=SCxxxx` at the call site instead (see individual
# scripts for those, each with its own justification comment).
#
# SC2034 (unused variable): builder scripts define intentional config/env vars
#   (RUN_TAG, GUEST_KEY, VMID bands, ...) that document the tile shape even when
#   a given build path doesn't read them.
# SC2054 (commas in array elements): QEMU command lines are arrays whose
#   elements legitimately contain commas (-device foo,bar=x) — systematic
#   false positive in tile launchers.
# SC2015 (`A && B || C` is not if/then/else): used pervasively and
#   deliberately across ~65 files as a compact "do X, else log/fallback Y"
#   idiom (install/build/coldboot/verify scripts). The pitfall (C also runs if
#   A succeeds but B fails) is real in the abstract, but rewriting every site
#   to `if/then/else` is a large, high-risk diff across scripts that build and
#   drive live VM tiles, for a benefit that's purely a possibly-misleading log
#   line in the vast majority of instances (the common shape is
#   `cond && action || log "fallback message"`, and the great majority of the
#   rest end in `|| true` — a no-op that only resets $? regardless of which
#   branch fired). Accepted repo-wide rather than touched file-by-file under
#   the "behavior-preserving only" rule for scripts that drive the live lab.
disable=SC2034,SC2054,SC2015
external-sources=true
